#pragma once
namespace dingosdk::vr::guide {
    struct Page { const char* title; const char* text; };
    inline constexpr Page pages[]{
        {"WELCOME TO RESKATE VR", "Choose LAUNCH VR for your headset or PLAY for the regular game. Connect Meta Quest Link / Air Link before launching VR.\n\nVR now stays in a square window: fullscreen and maximize are blocked. Change both dimensions together in Launcher Settings > VR > Square size. Smaller sizes cost less GPU time. Standard PLAY has separate display settings."},
        {"YOUR CONTROLS", "Default Quest layout: right A/B push, left X gets on/off the board, left Y stops. Grips grab. Left trigger is LB. Hold the right index trigger and move the left stick for the D-pad; release to steer normally.\n\nClick/release the left stick to switch first/third person. Click the right stick (or F8) to recenter while looking straight ahead. View switches reset the headset origin.\n\nYou can reassign buttons, triggers, stick clicks and short/hold menu gestures in ADDONS > VR > CONTROLS. Saved remaps replace these defaults."},
        {"MENUS AND INPUT SOURCE", "Short-press the hamburger menu for the game pause menu. Hold it about 0.6 seconds for ReSkate. In menus, point the right controller at the panel and pull its trigger to click or drag. Release before the first click after opening a menu.\n\nADDONS > VR > CONTROLS offers Quest controllers + gamepad or Regular gamepad only. A regular gamepad keeps working while head tracking stays on. With gamepad-only, open ReSkate using your configured menu key or regular controller binding (Settings > Keys / Controls).\n\nYou can also change the menu click button or turn the VR pointer off."},
        {"COMFORT, HUD AND SMOOTHNESS", "Hold the menu button, then open ADDONS > VR. Show game HUD enables scores/objectives. HUD area size defaults to 50% and can go down to 10% to bring indicators inwards.\n\nHead-centred tracking and Level horizon keep animation out of your view. Recenter after sitting/standing comfortably. Late head rotation should stay on for head turns.\n\nIf movement is choppy: try 72 Hz in Link, lower Launcher > VR square size and game graphics. Turn off frame generation, V-Sync and motion blur. VR eye resolution and Stereo search quality trade sharpness/edge quality for speed. Avoid changing FOV calibration to fix frame rate. Stop if the image is uncomfortable."},
        {"VOICE CHAT AND WHERE TO FIND HELP", "Enable voice chat in ONLINE > VOICE and select your microphone through Steam voice settings. In ADDONS > VR > CONTROLS, assign a Quest button to Voice talk and choose Hold to talk or Toggle to talk. The default leaves Voice talk unbound so it cannot transmit accidentally.\n\nIn VR the selected talk mode also works with your normal keyboard/controller push-to-talk binding in ONLINE > VOICE. Toggle: press once to talk, again to stop. Opening ReSkate menus, focus loss, disconnects, rebinding or leaving the session reset transmission; release before talking again. Open microphone mode is controlled separately in ONLINE > VOICE.\n\nReopen this guide any time from Launcher Settings > VR > Open VR tutorial. Button mappings and VR tuning save to your profile."}
    };
}
